sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Op as Operator screen
  participant S as Supervisor
  participant C as Screw
  Note over S,C: Robot is at spot 10, Screw step.<br/>A screw is loaded into fastening position,<br/>then the live camera must see the plate and screw<br/>both in the right spot, before fastening.
  S->>C: CMD_START (spot 10)
  C-->>S: FAULT (SCREW_NOT_IN_POSITION)
  S->>C: CMD_START (retry 1 of 2, reload and realign screw)
  C-->>S: FAULT (SCREW_NOT_IN_POSITION)
  S->>C: CMD_START (retry 2 of 2, reload and realign screw)
  C-->>S: FAULT (SCREW_NOT_IN_POSITION)
  S->>Op: ALERT: robot stopped. Spot 10, Screw, SCREW_NOT_IN_POSITION
  Note over S: Stack light turns flashing amber, so the operator sees it from across the roof
  Note over S: Robot waits at spot 10.<br/>Nothing moves.<br/>Operator can watch the live feed.
  alt Operator can fix it
    Op->>S: RESOLVED (fixed on the robot)
    S->>C: CMD_START (resume same step)
    C-->>S: DONE
    Note over S: Spot continues with the next step
  else Operator cannot fix it (last resort)
    Op->>S: SKIP_SPOT
    Note over S: Supervisor logs the spot as skipped, then advances to the next spot
  end
